 6 │ 
 7 │ Lifetime elisions are syntactic rules in Rust that allow the compiler to infer the lifetimes of reference parameters without explicit annotations, making code cleaner and more readable. These rules help maintain soundness while avoiding unnecessary verbosity.
   · ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   ·                                                                                                                                  ╰── machine-favored phrasing peaks at 'avoiding unnecessary verbosity.'
